From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:16:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 42/43] Dispersive extensions: packed line hooks for Debye,
 Lorentz and Drude cells

The line hooks of Engine_Ext_DebyeMaterial and
Engine_Ext_LorentzMaterial walked one position at a time through about
fifteen separate arrays (39 ns per Debye cell and 14 ns per Lorentz
cell on one thread).

Engine_Ext_Dispersive::SetupGroups now puts the positions of order 0,
sorted by x, into groups of up to four positions of one x-line, so a
group is never shared by two threads. Each group keeps its state and
its coefficients in one block and is updated four lanes at a time with
the same operations per lane as the scalar loops (the Debye
pre-update keeps its fused multiply-add). While a side is packed,
every hook of that side uses the blocks, so there is one copy of the
state. Packing is used by the multithreaded engine only and is skipped
when the blocks would need more than twice the memory of the field
arrays. OPENEMS_ADE_PACKED=0 keeps the old paths.

Results are bit-identical to the unpacked hooks and to v0.37.0:
probes, HDF5 dumps and raw fields on Lorentz, Drude, multi-pole Debye,
mixed and cylindrical cases at 1 to 15 threads, fused, unfused and
tiled.

